# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# What never leaves this folder.
#
# The repository is PRIVATE, but "private" is a setting someone can change by
# accident and a collaborator can be added to. Anything that would be a
# problem in public does not go in at all.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Dependencies and build output — Netlify installs and builds these itself.
node_modules/
dist/
.vite/

# ---- REAL STUDENT RECORDS. Never commit. ----
# A school grade report lives in this folder. Progress, grades and attendance
# live in the browser's database and in exported .json backups — none of it
# belongs in source control.
*.pdf
mission-control-progress-*.json
*-progress-*.json

# The whole Progress folder, whatever anything in it is called. (Aug 25, 2026.)
# She made this folder for his exports and imports. The three patterns above
# only catch the app's own download NAME — rename a file, drop in one Lamar
# saved himself, or copy one off his machine with a different name, and it
# would sit in GitHub Desktop ready to commit. The folder is the safer rule:
# a location cannot be typo'd the way a filename can.
Progress/
progress/

# The two other legal records the app can download. Neither was matched by any
# pattern above, anywhere in the repo — both carry his grades by name.
transcript-*.txt
homeschool-records-packet-*.txt

# ---- AND IT HAPPENED AGAIN, SIX DAYS LATER. (Sept 5, 2026.) ----
#
# Three exported databases were sitting COMMITTED in the repo root:
#
#   petal-pestle-backup-2026-08-31.json          177 KB
#   petal-pestle-backup-2026-08-31 (1).json      183 KB
#   petal-pestle-backup-2026-08-31 (1) (1).json  184 KB
#   petal-pestle-rendered.html
#
# Every rule above missed them, for two reasons at once. They are named
# "backup", and every pattern above only knew the word "progress". And they
# landed in the ROOT, not in Progress/, so the folder rule — added on Aug 25
# precisely because "a location cannot be typo'd the way a filename can" —
# never saw them either. The duplicate "(1)" names say how: a browser download
# saved to the repo folder rather than to Progress/.
#
# The lesson is the one this project keeps re-learning: a guard pinned to the
# NAME a thing happened to have will miss the same thing under another name.
# Guard the property. The property here is that an exported database is not
# source, and nothing in this repo needs loose JSON at the root — the build
# reads package.json and package-lock.json, and everything else lives under
# src/ or scripts/. So the root is closed by default and the two real files
# are named back in.
/*.json
!/package.json
!/package-lock.json

# And by shape, anywhere in the tree, for exports that land somewhere else.
*backup*.json
*-export-*.json
*-rendered.html

# Packaged copies of the app and working scratch.
*.zip
_build/
_to_delete/
src.backup-*/
.mc-patches/

# An empty stray directory from an old unzip.
mission-control-homeschool/

# OS and editor noise.
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.vscode/
.idea/
*.log
